Word: 村, Pinyin: cūn, Meaning: village, Example: 我们去了那个村。, Translation: We went to that village.

Word: 存, Pinyin: cún, Meaning: to exist; to deposit; to store; to keep; to survive, Example: 我存了很多钱。, Translation: I saved a lot of money.

Word: 存在, Pinyin: cún zài, Meaning: to exist; to be; existence, Example: 问题确实存在。, Translation: The problem really exists.

Word: 措施, Pinyin: cuò shī, Meaning: measure; step, Example: 我们需要采取措施。, Translation: We need to take measures.

Word: 错, Pinyin: Cuò, Meaning: surname Cuo, Example: 他姓错。, Translation: His surname is Cuo.

Word: 错过, Pinyin: cuò guò, Meaning: to miss (train, opportunity etc), Example: 我错过公交车了。, Translation: I missed the bus.

Word: 错误, Pinyin: cuò wù, Meaning: mistaken; false; wrong; error; mistake, Example: 我犯了个错误。, Translation: I made a mistake.

Word: 搭, Pinyin: dā, Meaning: to put up; to build (scaffolding); to hang (clothes on a pole); to connect; to join; to arrange in pairs; to match; to add; to throw in (resources); to take (boat, train); variant of 褡, Example: 我们一起搭车吧, Translation: Let's take a ride together.

Word: 达成, Pinyin: dá chéng, Meaning: to reach (an agreement); to accomplish, Example: 我们达成了协议。, Translation: We reached an agreement.

Word: 达到, Pinyin: dá dào, Meaning: to reach; to achieve; to attain, Example: 我达到了目标。, Translation: I reached my goal.

Word: 答, Pinyin: dā, Meaning: bound form having the same meaning as the free word 答, used in 答应, 理 etc, Example: 他答应帮我。, Translation: He promised to help me.

Word: 答案, Pinyin: dá àn, Meaning: answer; solution, Example: 你知道答案吗？, Translation: Do you know the answer?

Word: 答应, Pinyin: dā ying, Meaning: to answer; to respond; to answer positively; to agree; to accept; to promise, Example: 妈妈答应我了。, Translation: Mom promised me.

Word: 打, Pinyin: dá, Meaning: dozen (loanword), Example: 我买了一打鸡蛋。, Translation: I bought a dozen eggs.

Word: 打电话, Pinyin: dǎ diàn huà, Meaning: to make a telephone call, Example: 我明天打电话给你。, Translation: I will call you tomorrow.

Word: 打击, Pinyin: dǎ jī, Meaning: to hit; to strike; to attack; to crack down on sth; blow; (psychological) shock; percussion (music), Example: 别打击我的信心。, Translation: Don't crush my confidence.

Word: 打开, Pinyin: dǎ kāi, Meaning: to open; to show (a ticket); to turn on; to switch on, Example: 请打开窗户。, Translation: Please open the window.

Word: 打破, Pinyin: dǎ pò, Meaning: to break; to smash, Example: 他打破了花瓶。, Translation: He broke the vase.

Word: 打算, Pinyin: dǎ suàn, Meaning: to plan; to intend; to calculate; plan; intention; calculation, Example: 我打算去北京。, Translation: I plan to go to Beijing.

Word: 大, Pinyin: dà, Meaning: big; large; great; older (than another person); eldest (as in 姐); greatly; freely; fully; (dialect) father; (dialect) uncle (father's brother), Example: 他比我大两岁。, Translation: He is two years older than me.

Word: 大部分, Pinyin: dà bù fen, Meaning: in large part; the greater part; the majority, Example: 大部分人都来了。, Translation: Most people have come.

Word: 大大, Pinyin: dà dà, Meaning: greatly; enormously; (dialect) dad; uncle, Example: 这对我大大有帮助。, Translation: This greatly helps me.

Word: 大道, Pinyin: dà dào, Meaning: main street; avenue, Example: 我们沿大道走。, Translation: We walk along the main street.

Word: 大多数, Pinyin: dà duō shù, Meaning: (great) majority, Example: 大多数人喜欢喝茶。, Translation: Most people like drinking tea.

Word: 大概, Pinyin: dà gài, Meaning: roughly; probably; rough; approximate; about; general idea, Example: 大概几点到？, Translation: About what time will you arrive?

Word: 大哥, Pinyin: dà gē, Meaning: eldest brother; big brother (polite address for a man of about the same age as oneself); gang leader; boss, Example: 我大哥来了。, Translation: My eldest brother is here.

Word: 大会, Pinyin: dà huì, Meaning: general assembly; general meeting; convention, Example: 明天开大会。, Translation: We have a big meeting tomorrow.

Word: 大家, Pinyin: dà jiā, Meaning: everyone; influential family; great expert, Example: 大家明天见。, Translation: See everyone tomorrow.

Word: 大街, Pinyin: dà jiē, Meaning: street; main street, Example: 我们在大街上见面吧。, Translation: Let's meet on the main street.

Word: 大量, Pinyin: dà liàng, Meaning: great amount; large quantity; bulk; numerous; generous; magnanimous, Example: 我们买了大量水果。, Translation: We bought a large quantity of fruit.

Word: 大楼, Pinyin: dà lóu, Meaning: building (a relatively large, multistory one), Example: 他在大楼上班。, Translation: He works in the building.

Word: 大陆, Pinyin: Dà lù, Meaning: mainland China (reference to the PRC), Example: 我住在大陆。, Translation: I live in mainland China.

Word: 大门, Pinyin: Dà mén, Meaning: the Doors, US rock band, Example: 请关好大门。, Translation: Please close the main gate.

Word: 大脑, Pinyin: dà nǎo, Meaning: brain; cerebrum, Example: 大脑很重要。, Translation: The brain is very important.

Word: 大人, Pinyin: dà ren, Meaning: adult; grownup; title of respect toward superiors, Example: 他是大人。, Translation: He is an adult.

Word: 大赛, Pinyin: dà sài, Meaning: grand contest, Example: 他赢了大赛。, Translation: He won the contest.

Word: 大声, Pinyin: dà shēng, Meaning: loud voice; in a loud voice; loudly, Example: 请大声一点。, Translation: Please speak a little louder.

Word: 大师, Pinyin: dà shī, Meaning: great master; master, Example: 他是书法大师。, Translation: He is a calligraphy master.

Word: 大事, Pinyin: dà shì, Meaning: major event; major political event (war or change of regime); major social event (wedding or funeral); (do sth) in a big way, Example: 结婚是大事。, Translation: Marriage is a major event.

Word: 大厅, Pinyin: dà tīng, Meaning: hall; lounge, Example: 我们在大厅等你。, Translation: We are waiting for you in the hall.

Word: 大小, Pinyin: dà xiǎo, Meaning: dimension; magnitude; size; measurement; large and small; at any rate; adults and children; consideration of seniority, Example: 这个盒子的大小合适吗？, Translation: Is this box the right size?

Word: 大型, Pinyin: dà xíng, Meaning: large; large-scale, Example: 我们去了一个大型商场。, Translation: We went to a large mall.

Word: 大学, Pinyin: Dà xué, Meaning: the Great Learning, one of the Four Books 四书 in Confucianism, Example: 我最近在读大学。, Translation: I am currently reading The Great Learning.

Word: 大约, Pinyin: dà yuē, Meaning: approximately; probably, Example: 大约几点到？, Translation: About what time will you arrive?

Word: 大众, Pinyin: Dà zhòng, Meaning: Volkswagen (automobile manufacturer), Example: 他买了辆大众。, Translation: He bought a Volkswagen.

Word: 呆, Pinyin: dāi, Meaning: foolish; stupid; expressionless; blank; to stay, Example: 你发什么呆？, Translation: Why are you spacing out?

Word: 逮捕, Pinyin: dài bǔ, Meaning: to arrest; to apprehend; an arrest, Example: 警察逮捕了小偷。, Translation: The police arrested the thief.

Word: 代, Pinyin: dài, Meaning: to substitute; to act on behalf of others; to replace; generation; dynasty; age; period; (historical) era; (geological) eon, Example: 我代你去。, Translation: I'll go for you.

Word: 代表, Pinyin: dài biǎo, Meaning: representative; delegate; to represent; to stand for; on behalf of; in the name of, Example: 我代表大家谢谢你。, Translation: I thank you on behalf of everyone.

Word: 代价, Pinyin: dài jià, Meaning: price; cost; consideration (in share dealing), Example: 成功总要付出代价。, Translation: Success always comes at a cost.

Word: 代理, Pinyin: dài lǐ, Meaning: to act on behalf of sb in a responsible position; to act as an agent or proxy; surrogate; (computing) proxy, Example: 他代理我去开会。, Translation: He is going to the meeting on my behalf.

Word: 带, Pinyin: dài, Meaning: band; belt; girdle; ribbon; tire; area; zone; region; to wear; to carry; to take along; to bear (i.e. to have); to lead; to bring; to look after; to raise, Example: 我带伞了。, Translation: I brought an umbrella.

Word: 带来, Pinyin: dài lái, Meaning: to bring; (fig.) to bring about; to produce, Example: 他带来了礼物。, Translation: He brought a gift.

Word: 待, Pinyin: dāi, Meaning: to stay, Example: 你在这儿待着吧。, Translation: Just stay here.

Word: 贷款, Pinyin: dài kuǎn, Meaning: a loan; to provide a loan (e.g. bank); to raise a loan (from e.g. a bank), Example: 我想贷款买房。, Translation: I want to get a loan to buy a house.

Word: 袋, Pinyin: dài, Meaning: pouch; bag; sack; pocket, Example: 书在袋子里。, Translation: The book is in the bag.

Word: 戴, Pinyin: Dài, Meaning: surname Dai, Example: 我姓戴。, Translation: My surname is Dai.

Word: 单, Pinyin: Shàn, Meaning: surname Shan, Example: 我姓单。, Translation: My surname is Shan.

Word: 单独, Pinyin: dān dú, Meaning: alone; by oneself; on one's own, Example: 我想单独吃饭。, Translation: I want to eat alone.

Word: 单身, Pinyin: dān shēn, Meaning: unmarried; single, Example: 我现在是单身。, Translation: I am single now.

Word: 单位, Pinyin: dān wèi, Meaning: unit (of measure); unit (group of people as a whole); work unit (place of employment, esp. in the PRC prior to economic reform), Example: 你的单位在哪里？, Translation: Where is your workplace?

Word: 担心, Pinyin: dān xīn, Meaning: anxious; worried; uneasy; to worry; to be anxious, Example: 我担心你。, Translation: I'm worried about you.

Word: 但, Pinyin: dàn, Meaning: but; yet; however; still; merely; only; just, Example: 我想去，但没时间。, Translation: I want to go, but I have no time.

Word: 但是, Pinyin: dàn shì, Meaning: but; however, Example: 我想去，但是没时间。, Translation: I want to go, but I have no time.

Word: 弹, Pinyin: dàn, Meaning: crossball; bullet; shot; shell; ball, Example: 他装好子弹了。, Translation: He loaded the bullets.

Word: 蛋, Pinyin: Dàn, Meaning: variant of 蜑, Example: 吃个蛋吧。, Translation: Have an egg.

Word: 蛋糕, Pinyin: dàn gāo, Meaning: cake, Example: 我想吃蛋糕。, Translation: I want to eat cake.

Word: 当, Pinyin: dāng, Meaning: (onom.) dong; ding dong (bell), Example: 你当心点。, Translation: Be careful.

Word: 当成, Pinyin: dàng chéng, Meaning: to consider as; to take to be, Example: 我把你当成朋友。, Translation: I consider you a friend.

Word: 当初, Pinyin: dāng chū, Meaning: at that time; originally, Example: 当初我不该走。, Translation: I shouldn't have left back then.

Word: 当地, Pinyin: dāng dì, Meaning: local, Example: 当地美食很好吃。, Translation: Local food is delicious.

Word: 当年, Pinyin: dāng nián, Meaning: in those days; then; in those years; during that time, Example: 当年我住在北京。, Translation: I lived in Beijing back then.

Word: 当然, Pinyin: dāng rán, Meaning: only natural; as it should be; certainly; of course; without doubt, Example: 当然可以。, Translation: Of course.

Word: 当时, Pinyin: dāng shí, Meaning: then; at that time; while, Example: 他当时没来。, Translation: He didn't come at that time.

Word: 当事人, Pinyin: dāng shì rén, Meaning: persons involved or implicated; party (to an affair), Example: 当事人是谁？, Translation: Who is the person involved?

Word: 当天, Pinyin: dāng tiān, Meaning: on that day, Example: 我当天就回去了。, Translation: I went back on that day.

Word: 当中, Pinyin: dāng zhōng, Meaning: among; in the middle; in the center, Example: 他在我们当中。, Translation: He is among us.

Word: 当作, Pinyin: dàng zuò, Meaning: to treat as; to regard as, Example: 我把你当作朋友。, Translation: I treat you as a friend.

Word: 挡, Pinyin: dǎng, Meaning: to resist; to obstruct; to hinder; to keep off; to block (a blow); to get in the way of; cover; gear (e.g. in a car's transmission), Example: 请别挡着门。, Translation: Please don't block the door.

Word: 党, Pinyin: Dǎng, Meaning: surname Dang, Example: 我姓党。, Translation: I am surnamed Dang.

Word: 档, Pinyin: dǎng, Meaning: (Tw) variant of 挡, gear, Example: 请挂档。, Translation: Please shift gear.

Word: 档案, Pinyin: dàng àn, Meaning: file; record; archive, Example: 档案在抽屉里。, Translation: The file is in the drawer.

Word: 刀, Pinyin: Dāo, Meaning: surname Dao, Example: 请给我一把刀。, Translation: Please give me a knife.

Word: 导弹, Pinyin: dǎo dàn, Meaning: (guided) missile, Example: 他们发射了导弹。, Translation: They launched a missile.

Word: 导演, Pinyin: dǎo yǎn, Meaning: to direct; director (film etc), Example: 他是电影导演。, Translation: He is a film director.

Word: 导致, Pinyin: dǎo zhì, Meaning: to lead to; to create; to cause; to bring about, Example: 熬夜导致失眠。, Translation: Staying up late causes insomnia.

Word: 岛, Pinyin: dǎo, Meaning: variant of 岛, Example: 我们去岛上玩吧。, Translation: Let's go to the island to play.

Word: 到, Pinyin: dào, Meaning: to reach; to arrive; to leave for; to go to; to (a place); until (a time); up to (a point); (verb complement indicating arriving at a place or reaching a point); considerate; thoughtful; thorough, Example: 我到家了。, Translation: I've arrived home.

Word: 到处, Pinyin: dào chù, Meaning: everywhere, Example: 我到处找你。, Translation: I'm looking for you everywhere.

Word: 到达, Pinyin: dào dá, Meaning: to reach; to arrive, Example: 我们明天到达北京。, Translation: We arrive in Beijing tomorrow.

Word: 到底, Pinyin: dào dǐ, Meaning: finally; in the end; when all is said and done; after all; to the end; to the last, Example: 他到底来了。, Translation: He finally came.

Word: 到来, Pinyin: dào lái, Meaning: to arrive; arrival; advent, Example: 期待你的到来。, Translation: Looking forward to your arrival.

