Word: 就, Pinyin: jiù, Meaning: (after a suppositional clause) in that case; then; (after a clause of action) as soon as; immediately after; (same as 是) merely; nothing else but; simply; just; precisely; exactly; only; as little as; as much as; as many as; to approach; to move towards; to undertake; to engage in; (often followed by 着) taking advantage of; (of food) to go with; with regard to; concerning; (pattern: 就 ... 也 ...) even if ... still ...; (pattern: 不 ... 就 ...) if not ... then must be ..., Example: 那就走吧。, Translation: Then let's go.

Word: 就是, Pinyin: jiù shì, Meaning: exactly; precisely; only; simply; just; (used correlatively with 也) even; even if, Example: 我就是不知道。, Translation: I just don't know.

Word: 就算, Pinyin: jiù suàn, Meaning: (coll.) even if, Example: 就算贵，我也买。, Translation: Even if it's expensive, I'll buy it.

Word: 就要, Pinyin: jiù yào, Meaning: will; shall; to be going to, Example: 我明天就要出发。, Translation: I will leave tomorrow.

Word: 居民, Pinyin: jū mín, Meaning: resident; inhabitant, Example: 我们是本地居民。, Translation: We are local residents.

Word: 居然, Pinyin: jū rán, Meaning: unexpectedly; to one's surprise; go so far as to, Example: 他居然考了第一。, Translation: He actually got first place.

Word: 局, Pinyin: jú, Meaning: narrow, Example: 我们组一局吧。, Translation: Let's form a group.

Word: 局面, Pinyin: jú miàn, Meaning: aspect; phase; situation, Example: 现在局面很好。, Translation: The situation is good now.

Word: 局长, Pinyin: jú zhǎng, Meaning: bureau chief, Example: 局长来了。, Translation: The bureau chief has arrived.

Word: 举, Pinyin: jǔ, Meaning: variant of 举, Example: 请举手。, Translation: Please raise your hand.

Word: 举办, Pinyin: jǔ bàn, Meaning: to conduct; to hold, Example: 我们举办聚会。, Translation: We are holding a party.

Word: 举行, Pinyin: jǔ xíng, Meaning: to hold (a meeting, ceremony etc), Example: 明天举行会议。, Translation: A meeting will be held tomorrow.

Word: 巨大, Pinyin: jù dà, Meaning: huge; immense; very large; tremendous; gigantic; enormous, Example: 巨大的压力让我头疼, Translation: The huge pressure gives me a headache.

Word: 句, Pinyin: gōu, Meaning: variant of 勾, Example: 他用笔句了一条线。, Translation: He drew a line with his pen.

Word: 拒绝, Pinyin: jù jué, Meaning: to refuse; to decline; to reject, Example: 我拒绝了邀请。, Translation: I declined the invitation.

Word: 具体, Pinyin: jù tǐ, Meaning: concrete; definite; specific, Example: 请说具体点。, Translation: Please be more specific.

Word: 具有, Pinyin: jù yǒu, Meaning: to have; to possess, Example: 他具有信心。, Translation: He has confidence.

Word: 俱乐部, Pinyin: jù lè bù, Meaning: club (the organisation or its premises) (loanword), Example: 我们去俱乐部吧。, Translation: Let's go to the club.

Word: 剧, Pinyin: jù, Meaning: theatrical work (play, opera, TV series etc); dramatic (change, increase etc); acute; severe, Example: 你看什么剧？, Translation: What TV series are you watching?

Word: 据, Pinyin: jù, Meaning: variant of 据, Example: 据说他来了。, Translation: I heard he came.

Word: 据说, Pinyin: jù shuō, Meaning: it is said that; reportedly, Example: 据说明天放假。, Translation: It is said that tomorrow is a holiday.

Word: 距离, Pinyin: jù lí, Meaning: distance; to be apart from, Example: 这里的距离是多少？, Translation: What is the distance here?

Word: 聚, Pinyin: jù, Meaning: to congregate; to assemble; to mass; to gather together; to amass; to polymerize, Example: 大家周末聚一聚吧。, Translation: Let's get together on the weekend.

Word: 聚会, Pinyin: jù huì, Meaning: party; gathering; to meet; to get together, Example: 我们周末有个聚会。, Translation: We have a party this weekend.

Word: 卷, Pinyin: juǎn, Meaning: to roll up; roll; classifier for small rolled things (wad of paper money, movie reel etc), Example: 请把纸卷好。, Translation: Please roll up the paper.

Word: 决定, Pinyin: jué dìng, Meaning: to decide (to do something); to resolve; decision; certainly, Example: 我决定好了。, Translation: I've decided.

Word: 决赛, Pinyin: jué sài, Meaning: finals (of a competition), Example: 明天是决赛。, Translation: Tomorrow is the finals.

Word: 绝, Pinyin: jué, Meaning: to cut short; extinct; to disappear; to vanish; absolutely; by no means, Example: 他绝不可能来。, Translation: He absolutely won't come.

Word: 绝对, Pinyin: jué duì, Meaning: absolute; unconditional, Example: 我绝对同意。, Translation: I absolutely agree.

Word: 觉, Pinyin: jiào, Meaning: a nap; a sleep, Example: 我想睡午觉。, Translation: I want to take a nap.

Word: 觉得, Pinyin: jué de, Meaning: to think that ...; to feel that ...; to feel (uncomfortable etc), Example: 我觉得有点累。, Translation: I feel a bit tired.

Word: 军队, Pinyin: jūn duì, Meaning: armed forces; troops, Example: 我哥哥在军队。, Translation: My brother is in the army.

Word: 军事, Pinyin: jūn shì, Meaning: military affairs; (attributive) military, Example: 他喜欢军事。, Translation: He likes military affairs.

Word: 咖啡, Pinyin: kā fēi, Meaning: coffee (loanword), Example: 我喜欢喝咖啡。, Translation: I like drinking coffee.

Word: 卡, Pinyin: kǎ, Meaning: to stop; to block; (computing) (coll.) slow; (loanword) card; truck (from "car"); calorie (abbr. for 里); cassette, Example: 电脑太卡了。, Translation: The computer is too laggy.

Word: 开, Pinyin: kāi, Meaning: to open (transitive or intransitive); (of ships, vehicles, troops etc) to start; to turn on; to put in operation; to operate; to run; to boil; to write out (a prescription, check, invoice etc); (directional complement) away; off; carat (gold); abbr. for Kelvin, 开尔文; abbr. for 开本, book format, Example: 请开门。, Translation: Please open the door.

Word: 开车, Pinyin: kāi chē, Meaning: to drive a car, Example: 我每天开车上班。, Translation: I drive to work every day.

Word: 开发, Pinyin: kāi fā, Meaning: to exploit (a resource); to open up (for development); to develop, Example: 他在开发一款游戏。, Translation: He is developing a game.

Word: 开放, Pinyin: kāi fàng, Meaning: to bloom; to open; to be open (to the public); to open up (to the outside); to be open-minded; unrestrained by convention; unconstrained in one's sexuality, Example: 公园明天开放。, Translation: The park opens tomorrow.

Word: 开口, Pinyin: kāi kǒu, Meaning: to open one's mouth; to start to talk, Example: 他终于开口了。, Translation: He finally spoke.

Word: 开始, Pinyin: kāi shǐ, Meaning: to begin; beginning; to start; initial, Example: 我们开始吧。, Translation: Let's begin.

Word: 开玩笑, Pinyin: kāi wán xiào, Meaning: to play a joke; to make fun of; to joke, Example: 别开玩笑。, Translation: Don't joke.

Word: 开心, Pinyin: kāi xīn, Meaning: to feel happy; to rejoice; to have a great time; to make fun of sb, Example: 今天真开心。, Translation: I'm so happy today.

Word: 砍, Pinyin: kǎn, Meaning: to chop; to cut down; to throw sth at sb, Example: 爸爸砍柴。, Translation: Dad chops firewood.

Word: 看, Pinyin: kān, Meaning: to look after; to take care of; to watch; to guard, Example: 你帮我看着店。, Translation: Please watch the shop for me.

Word: 看出, Pinyin: kàn chū, Meaning: to make out; to see, Example: 你能看出区别吗？, Translation: Can you see the difference?

Word: 看到, Pinyin: kàn dào, Meaning: to see, Example: 我看到一只猫。, Translation: I see a cat.

Word: 看法, Pinyin: kàn fǎ, Meaning: way of looking at a thing; view; opinion, Example: 你的看法是什么？, Translation: What is your opinion?

Word: 看见, Pinyin: kàn jiàn, Meaning: to see; to catch sight of, Example: 你看见他了吗？, Translation: Did you see him?

Word: 看来, Pinyin: kàn lai, Meaning: apparently; it seems that, Example: 看来今天会下雨。, Translation: It seems it will rain today.

Word: 看起来, Pinyin: kàn qǐ lai, Meaning: seemingly; apparently; looks as if; appear to be; gives the impression that; seems on the face of it to be, Example: 看起来很好, Translation: It looks good.

Word: 看上去, Pinyin: kàn shang qu, Meaning: it would appear; it seems (that), Example: 他看上去很高兴。, Translation: He seems very happy.

Word: 考, Pinyin: kǎo, Meaning: to beat; to hit; variant of 考; to inspect; to test; to take an exam, Example: 我明天要考数学。, Translation: I'm taking a math exam tomorrow.

Word: 考虑, Pinyin: kǎo lǜ, Meaning: to think over; to consider; consideration, Example: 我在考虑。, Translation: I'm considering it.

Word: 考试, Pinyin: kǎo shì, Meaning: to take an exam; exam, Example: 我明天要考试。, Translation: I have an exam tomorrow.

Word: 考验, Pinyin: kǎo yàn, Meaning: to test; to put to the test; trial; ordeal, Example: 这真是场考验。, Translation: This is really a test.

Word: 烤, Pinyin: kǎo, Meaning: to roast; to bake; to broil, Example: 我喜欢烤面包。, Translation: I like to bake bread.

Word: 靠, Pinyin: kào, Meaning: to lean against or on; to stand by the side of; to come near to; to depend on; to trust; to fuck (vulgar); traditional military costume drama where the performers wear armor (old), Example: 我靠在墙上。, Translation: I lean against the wall.

Word: 靠近, Pinyin: kào jìn, Meaning: to be close to; to approach; to draw near, Example: 我们靠近点坐吧。, Translation: Let's sit a bit closer together.

Word: 科, Pinyin: kē, Meaning: branch of study; administrative section; division; field; branch; stage directions; family (taxonomy); rules; laws; to mete out (punishment); to levy (taxes etc); to fine sb, Example: 你学文科还是理科？, Translation: Do you study humanities or science?

Word: 科技, Pinyin: kē jì, Meaning: science and technology, Example: 科技让生活更好。, Translation: Technology makes life better.

Word: 科学, Pinyin: kē xué, Meaning: science; scientific knowledge; scientific; rational, Example: 我喜欢科学。, Translation: I like science.

Word: 科学家, Pinyin: kē xué jiā, Meaning: scientist, Example: 我想当科学家。, Translation: I want to be a scientist.

Word: 颗, Pinyin: kē, Meaning: classifier for small spheres, pearls, corn grains, teeth, hearts, satellites etc, Example: 我吃了一颗糖。, Translation: I ate a piece of candy.

Word: 可, Pinyin: kě, Meaning: (prefix) can; may; able to; -able; to approve; to permit; to suit; (particle used for emphasis) certainly; very, Example: 可以吗？, Translation: Is that okay?

Word: 可爱, Pinyin: kě ài, Meaning: adorable; cute; lovely, Example: 小猫很可爱。, Translation: The kitten is very cute.

Word: 可怜, Pinyin: kě lián, Meaning: pitiful; pathetic; to have pity on, Example: 这只小猫真可怜。, Translation: This little cat is so pitiful.

Word: 可能, Pinyin: kě néng, Meaning: might (happen); possible; probable; possibility; probability; maybe; perhaps, Example: 明天可能下雨。, Translation: It might rain tomorrow.

Word: 可怕, Pinyin: kě pà, Meaning: awful; dreadful; fearful; formidable; frightful; scary; hideous; horrible; terrible; terribly, Example: 这个电影很可怕。, Translation: This movie is very scary.

Word: 可是, Pinyin: kě shì, Meaning: but; however; (used for emphasis) indeed, Example: 我想去，可是没时间。, Translation: I want to go, but I have no time.

Word: 可惜, Pinyin: kě xī, Meaning: it is a pity; what a pity; unfortunately, Example: 可惜没买到票。, Translation: It's a pity I couldn't buy the ticket.

Word: 可以, Pinyin: kě yǐ, Meaning: can; may; possible; able to; not bad; pretty good, Example: 这样可以吗？, Translation: Is this okay?

Word: 渴望, Pinyin: kě wàng, Meaning: to thirst for; to long for, Example: 我渴望回家。, Translation: I long to go home.

Word: 克, Pinyin: Kè, Meaning: abbr. for 克罗地亚, Croatia; (Tw) abbr. for 克罗埃西亚, Croatia, Example: 你支持克吗？, Translation: Do you support Croatia?

Word: 刻, Pinyin: kè, Meaning: quarter (hour); moment; to carve; to engrave; to cut; oppressive; classifier for short time intervals, Example: 三点一刻开会。, Translation: We have a meeting at 3:15.

Word: 客户, Pinyin: kè hù, Meaning: client; customer, Example: 我的客户很多。, Translation: I have many customers.

Word: 客人, Pinyin: kè rén, Meaning: visitor; guest; customer; client, Example: 我家来了客人。, Translation: We have a guest at home.

Word: 课, Pinyin: kè, Meaning: subject; course; class; lesson; to levy; tax; form of divination, Example: 今天上什么课？, Translation: What class do we have today?

Word: 课程, Pinyin: kè chéng, Meaning: course; academic program, Example: 我喜欢这门课程。, Translation: I like this course.

Word: 肯, Pinyin: kěn, Meaning: old variant of 肯, Example: 他肯帮忙吗？, Translation: Will he be willing to help?

Word: 肯定, Pinyin: kěn dìng, Meaning: to be certain; to be positive; assuredly; definitely; to give recognition; to affirm; affirmative (answer), Example: 他肯定知道。, Translation: He definitely knows.

Word: 坑, Pinyin: kēng, Meaning: pit; depression; hollow; tunnel; hole in the ground; (archaic) to bury alive; to hoodwink; to cheat (sb), Example: 地上有个大坑。, Translation: There's a big pit on the ground.

Word: 空, Pinyin: kōng, Meaning: empty; air; sky; in vain, Example: 杯子是空的。, Translation: The cup is empty.

Word: 空间, Pinyin: kōng jiān, Meaning: space; room; (fig.) scope; leeway; (astronomy) outer space; (physics, math.) space, Example: 这里空间不够。, Translation: There isn't enough space here.

Word: 空气, Pinyin: kōng qì, Meaning: air; atmosphere, Example: 今天的空气真好。, Translation: The air is really nice today.

Word: 空中, Pinyin: kōng zhōng, Meaning: in the sky; in the air, Example: 小鸟在空中飞。, Translation: The little bird is flying in the sky.

Word: 恐怖, Pinyin: kǒng bù, Meaning: terrible; frightful; frightening; terror; terrorist, Example: 这部电影很恐怖。, Translation: This movie is very scary.

Word: 恐惧, Pinyin: kǒng jù, Meaning: to be frightened; fear; dread, Example: 恐惧让我睡不着。, Translation: Fear keeps me awake.

Word: 恐怕, Pinyin: kǒng pà, Meaning: fear; to dread; I'm afraid that...; perhaps; maybe, Example: 恐怕来不及了。, Translation: I'm afraid it's too late.

Word: 控制, Pinyin: kòng zhì, Meaning: to control, Example: 请控制音量。, Translation: Please control the volume.

Word: 口, Pinyin: kǒu, Meaning: mouth; classifier for things with mouths (people, domestic animals, cannons, wells etc); classifier for bites or mouthfuls, Example: 我家有三口人。, Translation: There are three people in my family.

Word: 扣, Pinyin: kòu, Meaning: to fasten; to button; button; buckle; knot; to arrest; to confiscate; to deduct (money); discount; to knock; to smash, spike or dunk (a ball); to cover (with a bowl etc); (fig.) to tag a label on sb; (Tw) (loanword) code, Example: 扣好安全带。, Translation: Please fasten your seatbelt.

Word: 哭, Pinyin: kū, Meaning: to cry; to weep, Example: 别哭了。, Translation: Don't cry.

Word: 苦, Pinyin: kǔ, Meaning: bitter; hardship; pain; to suffer; to bring suffering to; painstakingly, Example: 这药太苦了。, Translation: This medicine is too bitter.

Word: 库, Pinyin: kù, Meaning: warehouse; storehouse; (file) library, Example: 我们去库房吧。, Translation: Let's go to the warehouse.

Word: 裤子, Pinyin: kù zi, Meaning: variant of 裤子, trousers; pants, Example: 我的裤子破了。, Translation: My pants are torn.

Word: 酷, Pinyin: kù, Meaning: ruthless; strong (e.g. of wine); (loanword) cool; hip, Example: 这电影真酷。, Translation: This movie is really cool.

Word: 块, Pinyin: kuài, Meaning: lump; chunk; piece; classifier for pieces of cloth, cake, soap etc; (coll.) classifier for money and currency units, Example: 给我一块蛋糕。, Translation: Give me a piece of cake.

Word: 快, Pinyin: kuài, Meaning: rapid; quick; speed; rate; soon; almost; to make haste; clever; sharp (of knives or wits); forthright; plainspoken; gratified; pleased; pleasant, Example: 他跑得很快。, Translation: He runs very fast.

Word: 快乐, Pinyin: kuài lè, Meaning: happy; joyful, Example: 我很快乐。, Translation: I am very happy.

Word: 快速, Pinyin: kuài sù, Meaning: fast; high-speed; rapid, Example: 请快速回复我。, Translation: Please reply to me quickly.

Word: 宽, Pinyin: Kuān, Meaning: surname Kuan, Example: 我姓宽。, Translation: My surname is Kuan.

Word: 狂, Pinyin: kuáng, Meaning: mad; wild; violent, Example: 他太狂了。, Translation: He's too wild.

Word: 困, Pinyin: kùn, Meaning: to trap; to surround; hard-pressed; stranded; destitute, Example: 我们被困住了。, Translation: We are stuck.

Word: 困难, Pinyin: kùn nan, Meaning: difficult; challenging; straitened circumstances; difficult situation, Example: 有困难找我。, Translation: If you have any difficulties, let me know.

Word: 扩大, Pinyin: kuò dà, Meaning: to expand; to enlarge; to broaden one's scope, Example: 让我们扩大视野。, Translation: Let's broaden our horizons.

Word: 垃圾, Pinyin: lā jī, Meaning: trash; refuse; garbage; (coll.) of poor quality; Taiwan pr. [lè sè], Example: 地上有垃圾。, Translation: There is trash on the ground.

Word: 拉, Pinyin: lā, Meaning: to pull; to play (a bowed instrument); to drag; to draw; to chat; (coll.) to empty one's bowels, Example: 别拉我的手。, Translation: Don't pull my hand.

Word: 辣, Pinyin: là, Meaning: old variant of 辣, Example: 这菜太辣了。, Translation: This dish is too spicy.

Word: 啦, Pinyin: lā, Meaning: (onom.) sound of singing, cheering etc; (phonetic); (dialect) to chat, Example: 我走啦！, Translation: I'm leaving!

Word: 啦啦队, Pinyin: lā lā duì, Meaning: cheerleading squad, Example: 啦啦队在看台上。, Translation: The cheerleading squad is on the bleachers.

Word: 来, Pinyin: lái, Meaning: to come; (used as a substitute for a more specific verb); hither (directional complement for motion toward the speaker, as in 回来); ever since (as in 自古以来); for the past (amount of time); (prefix) the coming ...; the next ... (as in 来世); (between two verbs) in order to; (after a round number) approximately; (used after 得 to indicate possibility, as in 谈得来, or after 不 to indicate impossibility, as in 吃不来), Example: 明天我来。, Translation: I'll come tomorrow.

Word: 来到, Pinyin: lái dào, Meaning: to arrive; to come, Example: 我来到学校。, Translation: I came to school.

Word: 来源, Pinyin: lái yuán, Meaning: source (of information etc); origin, Example: 这个信息的来源是什么？, Translation: What is the source of this information?

Word: 来自, Pinyin: lái zì, Meaning: to come from (a place); From: (in email header), Example: 我来自北京。, Translation: I come from Beijing.

Word: 蓝, Pinyin: Lán, Meaning: surname Lan, Example: 我朋友姓蓝。, Translation: My friend's surname is Lan.

Word: 蓝色, Pinyin: lán sè, Meaning: blue (color), Example: 我喜欢蓝色。, Translation: I like blue.

Word: 篮球, Pinyin: lán qiú, Meaning: basketball, Example: 我喜欢打篮球。, Translation: I like playing basketball.

Word: 烂, Pinyin: làn, Meaning: soft; mushy; well-cooked and soft; to rot; to decompose; rotten; worn out; chaotic; messy; utterly; thoroughly; crappy; bad, Example: 水果烂了。, Translation: The fruit is rotten.

Word: 狼, Pinyin: láng, Meaning: wolf, Example: 我看见一只狼。, Translation: I saw a wolf.

Word: 浪费, Pinyin: làng fèi, Meaning: to waste; to squander, Example: 不要浪费食物。, Translation: Don't waste food.

Word: 浪漫, Pinyin: làng màn, Meaning: romantic, Example: 这很浪漫。, Translation: This is very romantic.

Word: 老, Pinyin: lǎo, Meaning: prefix used before the surname of a person or a numeral indicating the order of birth of the children in a family or to indicate affection or familiarity; old (of people); venerable (person); experienced; of long standing; always; all the time; of the past; very; outdated; (of meat etc) tough, Example: 他是个老人。, Translation: He is an old man.

Word: 老板, Pinyin: lǎo bǎn, Meaning: variant of 老板, Example: 老板在哪里？, Translation: Where is the boss?

Word: 老大, Pinyin: lǎo dà, Meaning: old age; very; eldest child in a family; leader of a group; boss; captain of a boat; leader of a criminal gang, Example: 他是家里的老大。, Translation: He is the eldest child in the family.

Word: 老公, Pinyin: lǎo gōng, Meaning: (coll.) husband, Example: 我老公在家。, Translation: My husband is at home.

Word: 老婆, Pinyin: lǎo pó, Meaning: (coll.) wife, Example: 我老婆很漂亮。, Translation: My wife is very pretty.

Word: 老人, Pinyin: lǎo rén, Meaning: old man or woman; the elderly; one's aged parents or grandparents, Example: 公园里有位老人。, Translation: There is an old man in the park.

Word: 老师, Pinyin: lǎo shī, Meaning: teacher, Example: 你是老师吗？, Translation: Are you a teacher?

Word: 乐, Pinyin: Lè, Meaning: surname Le, Example: 我姓乐。, Translation: My surname is Le.

Word: 乐队, Pinyin: yuè duì, Meaning: band; pop group, Example: 我喜欢这个乐队。, Translation: I like this band.

Word: 了, Pinyin: le, Meaning: (completed action marker); (modal particle indicating change of state, situation now); (modal particle intensifying preceding clause), Example: 我吃饭了。, Translation: I've eaten.

Word: 了解, Pinyin: liǎo jiě, Meaning: to understand; to realize; to find out, Example: 我想了解一下。, Translation: I'd like to know more about it.

Word: 勒, Pinyin: lè, Meaning: to rein in; to compel; to force; to carve; to engrave; (literary) to command; to lead; bridle; (physics) abbr. for 斯, lux, Example: 别勒太紧。, Translation: Don't pull it too tight.

Word: 雷, Pinyin: Léi, Meaning: surname Lei, Example: 他姓雷。, Translation: His surname is Lei.

Word: 类, Pinyin: lèi, Meaning: kind; type; class; category; similar; like; to resemble, Example: 这类书很有趣。, Translation: This kind of book is interesting.

Word: 类似, Pinyin: lèi sì, Meaning: similar; analogous, Example: 这两个故事类似。, Translation: These two stories are similar.

Word: 类型, Pinyin: lèi xíng, Meaning: type; kind; category; (computer programming) type, Example: 这是什么类型？, Translation: What type is this?

Word: 累, Pinyin: lěi, Meaning: to accumulate; to involve or implicate (Taiwan pr. [lèi]); continuous; repeated, Example: 别连累我。, Translation: Don't drag me into it.

Word: 冷, Pinyin: Lěng, Meaning: surname Leng, Example: 我朋友姓冷。, Translation: My friend's surname is Leng.

Word: 冷静, Pinyin: lěng jìng, Meaning: calm; cool-headed; dispassionate; (of a place) deserted; quiet, Example: 请冷静一下。, Translation: Please calm down.

Word: 离, Pinyin: chī, Meaning: mythical beast (archaic), Example: 传说里有一种叫离的兽。, Translation: Legends mention an archaic mythical beast called Li.

Word: 离婚, Pinyin: lí hūn, Meaning: to divorce, Example: 他们想离婚。, Translation: They want to divorce.

Word: 离开, Pinyin: lí kāi, Meaning: to depart; to leave, Example: 我要离开了。, Translation: I'm leaving now.

