Word: 其实, Pinyin: qí shí, Meaning: actually; in fact; really, Example: 其实我不饿。, Translation: Actually, I'm not hungry.

Word: 其他, Pinyin: qí tā, Meaning: other; (sth or sb) else; the rest, Example: 我要这个，其他不要。, Translation: I want this one, not the others.

Word: 其中, Pinyin: qí zhōng, Meaning: among; in; included among these, Example: 五本书，其中一本丢了。, Translation: Of the five books, one is missing.

Word: 奇怪, Pinyin: qí guài, Meaning: strange; odd; to marvel; to be baffled, Example: 这事真奇怪。, Translation: This is really strange.

Word: 奇迹, Pinyin: qí jì, Meaning: miracle; miraculous; wonder; marvel, Example: 这是一个奇迹。, Translation: This is a miracle.

Word: 骑, Pinyin: jì, Meaning: (Tw) saddle horse; mounted soldier, Example: 他骑马打仗。, Translation: He fights on horseback.

Word: 企业, Pinyin: qǐ yè, Meaning: company; firm; enterprise; corporation, Example: 我在一家企业工作。, Translation: I work at a company.

Word: 启动, Pinyin: qǐ dòng, Meaning: to start (a machine); (fig.) to set in motion; to launch (an operation); to activate (a plan), Example: 我们启动计划吧。, Translation: Let's launch the plan.

Word: 起, Pinyin: qǐ, Meaning: to rise; to raise; to get up; to set out; to start; to appear; to launch; to initiate (action); to draft; to establish; to get (from a depot or counter); verb suffix, to start; starting from (a time, place, price etc); classifier for occurrences or unpredictable events: case, instance; classifier for groups: batch, group, Example: 我起床了。, Translation: I got up.

Word: 起床, Pinyin: qǐ chuáng, Meaning: to get out of bed; to get up, Example: 你几点起床？, Translation: What time do you get up?

Word: 起来, Pinyin: qǐ lai, Meaning: to stand up; to get up; also pr. [qǐ lái], Example: 他站起来。, Translation: He stands up.

Word: 起诉, Pinyin: qǐ sù, Meaning: to sue; to bring a lawsuit against; to prosecute, Example: 我要起诉他, Translation: I want to sue him.

Word: 气, Pinyin: qì, Meaning: gas; air; smell; weather; to make angry; to annoy; to get angry; vital energy; qi, Example: 我有点生气。, Translation: I am a little angry.

Word: 气氛, Pinyin: qì fēn, Meaning: atmosphere; mood, Example: 今天的气氛很好。, Translation: The atmosphere today is very good.

Word: 汽车, Pinyin: qì chē, Meaning: car; automobile; bus, Example: 我坐汽车去学校。, Translation: I take the car to school.

Word: 千, Pinyin: qiān, Meaning: thousand, Example: 我有一千块钱。, Translation: I have a thousand yuan.

Word: 千万, Pinyin: qiān wàn, Meaning: ten million; countless; many; one must by all means, Example: 千万别迟到。, Translation: Absolutely don't be late.

Word: 牵, Pinyin: qiān, Meaning: to lead along; to pull (an animal on a tether); (bound form) to involve; to draw in, Example: 妈妈牵着我的手。, Translation: Mom holds my hand.

Word: 签, Pinyin: qiān, Meaning: to sign one's name; to write brief comments on a document; inscribed bamboo stick (variant of 签); visa, Example: 请在这里签。, Translation: Please sign here.

Word: 签名, Pinyin: qiān míng, Meaning: to sign (one's name with a pen etc); to autograph; signature, Example: 请在这里签名。, Translation: Please sign here.

Word: 前, Pinyin: qián, Meaning: front; forward; ahead; first; top (followed by a number); future; ago; before; BC (e.g. 前293年); former; formerly, Example: 我在前面等你。, Translation: I'll wait for you ahead.

Word: 前进, Pinyin: qián jìn, Meaning: to go forward; to forge ahead; to advance; onward, Example: 我们继续前进。, Translation: Let's keep moving forward.

Word: 前面, Pinyin: qián miàn, Meaning: ahead; in front; preceding; above; also pr. [qián mian], Example: 请坐前面。, Translation: Please sit in the front.

Word: 前往, Pinyin: qián wǎng, Meaning: to leave for; to proceed towards; to go to, Example: 我明天前往北京。, Translation: I am going to Beijing tomorrow.

