Word: 轻易, Pinyin: qīng yì, Meaning: easily; lightly; rashly, Example: 别轻易相信别人。, Translation: Don't trust others easily.

Word: 倾向, Pinyin: qīng xiàng, Meaning: trend; tendency; orientation, Example: 他有当老师的倾向。, Translation: He has a tendency to become a teacher.

Word: 清, Pinyin: Qīng, Meaning: Qing (Wade-Giles: Ch'ing) dynasty of imperial China (1644-1911); surname Qing, Example: 他喜欢清朝。, Translation: He likes the Qing dynasty.

Word: 清楚, Pinyin: qīng chu, Meaning: clear; distinct; to understand thoroughly; to be clear about, Example: 请说清楚点。, Translation: Please speak more clearly.

Word: 清理, Pinyin: qīng lǐ, Meaning: to clear up; to tidy up; to dispose of, Example: 我要清理房间。, Translation: I need to clean up the room.

Word: 清醒, Pinyin: qīng xǐng, Meaning: clear-headed; sober; awake, Example: 我需要清醒一下。, Translation: I need to clear my head.

Word: 情, Pinyin: qíng, Meaning: feeling; emotion; passion; situation, Example: 他对我有情, Translation: He has feelings for me.

Word: 情报, Pinyin: qíng bào, Meaning: information; intelligence, Example: 我收到了重要情报。, Translation: I received important intelligence.

Word: 情感, Pinyin: qíng gǎn, Meaning: feeling; emotion; to move (emotionally), Example: 这种情感很真实。, Translation: This feeling is very real.

Word: 情况, Pinyin: qíng kuàng, Meaning: circumstances; state of affairs; situation, Example: 情况怎么样？, Translation: How is the situation?

Word: 情绪, Pinyin: qíng xù, Meaning: mood; state of mind; moodiness, Example: 他今天情绪不好。, Translation: He's in a bad mood today.

Word: 请, Pinyin: qǐng, Meaning: to ask; to invite; please (do sth); to treat (to a meal etc); to request, Example: 请你吃饭。, Translation: I will treat you to a meal.

Word: 请求, Pinyin: qǐng qiú, Meaning: to request; to ask; request, Example: 我请求帮忙。, Translation: I request help.

Word: 请问, Pinyin: qǐng wèn, Meaning: Excuse me, may I ask...?, Example: 请问厕所在哪里？, Translation: Excuse me, where is the restroom?

Word: 庆祝, Pinyin: qìng zhù, Meaning: to celebrate, Example: 我们庆祝生日。, Translation: We are celebrating a birthday.

Word: 求, Pinyin: qiú, Meaning: to seek; to look for; to request; to demand; to beseech, Example: 我求你帮帮我。, Translation: I'm begging you to help me.

Word: 球, Pinyin: qiú, Meaning: ball; sphere; globe; ball game; match, Example: 我要买一个球。, Translation: I want to buy a ball.

Word: 球队, Pinyin: qiú duì, Meaning: sports team (basketball, soccer, football etc), Example: 我们球队赢了。, Translation: Our team won.

Word: 球员, Pinyin: qiú yuán, Meaning: (ball sports) player; team member, Example: 这位球员很强。, Translation: This player is very strong.

Word: 区, Pinyin: Oū, Meaning: surname Ou, Example: 我姓区。, Translation: My surname is Ou.

Word: 区别, Pinyin: qū bié, Meaning: difference; to distinguish; to discriminate; to make a distinction, Example: 它们有什么区别？, Translation: What's the difference between them?

Word: 区域, Pinyin: qū yù, Meaning: area; region; district, Example: 这个区域很安静。, Translation: This area is very quiet.

Word: 曲, Pinyin: Qū, Meaning: surname Qu, Example: 他姓曲。, Translation: His surname is Qu.

Word: 取, Pinyin: qǔ, Meaning: to take; to get; to choose; to fetch, Example: 我去银行取钱。, Translation: I'm going to the bank to get some money.

Word: 取得, Pinyin: qǔ dé, Meaning: to acquire; to get; to obtain, Example: 我取得了好成绩。, Translation: I got good grades.

Word: 取消, Pinyin: qǔ xiāo, Meaning: to cancel; cancellation, Example: 请取消会议。, Translation: Please cancel the meeting.

Word: 娶, Pinyin: qǔ, Meaning: to take a wife; to marry (a woman), Example: 他打算娶她。, Translation: He plans to marry her.

Word: 去, Pinyin: qù, Meaning: to go; to go to (a place); (of a time etc) last; just passed; to send; to remove; to get rid of; to reduce; to be apart from in space or time; to die (euphemism); to play (a part); (when used either before or after a verb) to go in order to do sth; (after a verb of motion indicates movement away from the speaker); (used after certain verbs to indicate detachment or separation), Example: 你去哪里？, Translation: Where are you going?

Word: 去年, Pinyin: qù nián, Meaning: last year, Example: 去年我去北京。, Translation: Last year I went to Beijing.

Word: 去世, Pinyin: qù shì, Meaning: to pass away; to die, Example: 爷爷去年去世了。, Translation: Grandpa passed away last year.

Word: 圈, Pinyin: juān, Meaning: to confine; to lock up; to pen in, Example: 他把羊圈起来了。, Translation: He penned the sheep up.

Word: 全, Pinyin: Quán, Meaning: surname Quan, Example: 我姓全。, Translation: My surname is Quan.

Word: 全部, Pinyin: quán bù, Meaning: whole; all, Example: 全部在这里。, Translation: Everything is here.

